The "Cell Renderer" snippet imports `GridCellRenderer` from `@object-ui/fields`, but there is no such export defined in `packages/fields/src/index.tsx` (the standard map uses an inline fallback for `grid`). This example will fail if copied directly; please either add a concrete `GridCellRenderer` export or update the docs to use the supported pattern, such as `getCellRenderer('grid')`.
```suggestion
import { getCellRenderer } from '@object-ui/fields';

const GridCellRenderer = getCellRenderer('grid');
```

The "Validation" section states that the Location field validates coordinate ranges (e.g., rejecting latitude 95 or longitude 200), but the current `LocationField` implementation only parses the two numbers and does not enforce any min/max range. Either add client-side range validation to `LocationField` or adjust this documentation to avoid promising behavior that is not implemented.
```suggestion
By default, the `LocationField` only parses the two numeric values and does **not** enforce latitude/longitude ranges.
You should add your own validation (client-side or server-side) to ensure coordinates are within acceptable bounds
(typically latitude ∈ [-90, 90], longitude ∈ [-180, 180]).

```typescript
// Example validation helper (not built into LocationField)
function isValidLocation(value?: { latitude: number; longitude: number }) {
  if (!value) return false;

  const { latitude, longitude } = value;

  const isLatitudeValid = latitude >= -90 && latitude <= 90;
  const isLongitudeValid = longitude >= -180 && longitude <= 180;

  return isLatitudeValid && isLongitudeValid;
}

// Valid coordinates
isValidLocation({ latitude: 37.7749, longitude: -122.4194 }); // true

// Invalid - latitude out of range
isValidLocation({ latitude: 95, longitude: -122.4194 }); // false

// Invalid - longitude out of range
isValidLocation({ latitude: 37.7749, longitude: 200 }); // false
```

The "Cell Renderer" example imports `VectorCellRenderer` from `@object-ui/fields`, but there is no such export in `packages/fields/src/index.tsx` (only a generic fallback renderer is registered for `vector`). This sample will not compile as written; either export a real `VectorCellRenderer` or change the example to use `getCellRenderer('vector')` or the appropriate existing API.
```suggestion
In tables/grids, the `vector` field uses the registered `"vector"` cell renderer to display a compact preview:

```typescript
// Example column definition using the built-in "vector" cell renderer
const columns = [
  {
    field: 'embedding',
    headerName: 'Embedding',
    cellRenderer: 'vector',
  },
];
```

The "Cell Renderer" section shows `import { ObjectCellRenderer } from '@object-ui/fields';`, but there is no `ObjectCellRenderer` export in the fields package (the standard map uses an inline fallback for `object` instead). This example will not work as written; please either introduce an exported `ObjectCellRenderer` or update the docs to refer to the actual API (for example, `getCellRenderer('object')`).
```suggestion
import { getCellRenderer } from '@object-ui/fields';

const ObjectCellRenderer = getCellRenderer('object');

// In a table/grid column definition:
const columns = [
  {
    key: 'metadata',
    header: 'Metadata',
    cell: ObjectCellRenderer,
  },
];

// Renders a compact "[Object]" or truncated JSON preview in read-only mode
```

The "Cell Renderer" example imports `SummaryCellRenderer` from `@object-ui/fields`, but that symbol is not exported from `packages/fields/src/index.tsx` (summary currently reuses `FormulaCellRenderer`). To avoid broken examples, either add an exported `SummaryCellRenderer` or adjust the documentation to reference the existing `FormulaCellRenderer` or `getCellRenderer('summary')` API.
```suggestion
import { getCellRenderer } from '@object-ui/fields';

const SummaryCellRenderer = getCellRenderer('summary');
```
